================================================================================
Bundled data
================================================================================

The datasets below are public domain. Attribution is not required; it is given
because knowing where the data came from matters.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Lichess puzzle database — CC0 1.0 (public domain)
https://database.lichess.org/#puzzles
Provided by Lichess

Roughly 6.1 million theme-tagged, rated puzzles. Downloaded and imported by the
user; not redistributed in this repository.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
lichess-org/chess-openings — CC0 1.0 (public domain)
https://github.com/lichess-org/chess-openings
Provided by Lichess

Opening names keyed by move sequence. Roughly 3,800 named lines across five TSV
files, redistributed unmodified in this repository at src/ingest/openings-data/
and imported into the local database on first run. As a collection of facts the
dataset is in the public domain, dedicated under CC0 1.0; no attribution is
required, and this entry is recorded for provenance.

================================================================================
Derived ideas
================================================================================

The tactical motif detectors are an independent reimplementation of the
heuristics described in lichess-puzzler's cook.py, which is AGPL-3.0 licensed.
The ideas are reused; no code was copied. Motif identifiers deliberately match
Lichess's theme vocabulary so that puzzle matching is a direct lookup.
